<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="utf-8" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, shrink-to-fit=no" />
        <title>Online Exam Instructions</title>
        <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Ubuntu&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/bootstrap.min.css" />
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/style.css" />
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/instructions.css" />
    </head>
    <body>
        <div class="container-fluid">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="col-lg-12 col-md-12">
                        <div class="main-heading">
                            <h1>Online Exam Instructions</h1>
                        </div>
                        <div class="profile-card" style="margin-top: 50px;">
                            <div class="instruction">
                                <ul>
                                    <li>Please read the instructions carefully, and click 'I am ready to begin' button to start the exam.;</li>
                                    <li>Each question id followed by 4 alternatives / options for MCQ question only.</li>
                                    <li>
                                        The language shall be English Only <br />
                                        After click on the <b>'I am ready to begin'</b> button the actual test time will begin;
                                    </li>
                                    <li>The candidates no need to accept the Language. the question will be available in english only.</li>
                                    <li>Only one question will be displayed at a time;</li>
                                    <li>In order to answer a question, the candidate should 'mouse click' the option they think is appropriate / correct;</li>
                                    <li>The alternative which has been clicked on will be highlighted and shall be treated as the answer given by the candidate for the question;</li>
                                    <li>
                                        After selecting an answer for a question the candidate should click on the <span class="save">Save & Next >></span> Button to save the answer and proceed to the next question. The candidate should
                                        note that without clicking on <span class="save">Save & Next >></span> button the answer selected for a question will not be saved;
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        In case a candidate does not wish to attempt the question than he / she should not click on any option for the question. A candidate can choose to deselect his / her answer for a particular question
                                        by clicking on the <span class="clear-response">Clear Response</span> button provided against each question;
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        In case a candidate want to skip a particular question and return to it later before submitting his / her test or a candidate 'click' (select) an answer for a particular question but wishes to review
                                        it later, he / she may note down the question number on the sheet provided. In such case the candidate may also click on the <span class="save-marked">Save & Mark</span> button. In case an answer has
                                        been selected for a particularquestion which has been marked as <span class="save-marked">Save & Mark</span>, the answer marked will be taken for final evaluation;
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        The question number of attempted and unattemped question are also shown to the right of the screen. A candidate can then click on any of the question number to view the question, in order to attempt /
                                        revise his / her answer to the question;
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        The candidate shall not be allowed to enter the examination hall half-an-hour after the commencement of the examination, and shall be permitted to leave the hall only after the first half-an-hour from
                                        the commencement of the examination.
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        A candidate can navigate between questions by clicking on the question number displayed to the right of the screen or also use <span class="previous"><< Previous</span> button and
                                        <span class="save">Save & Next >></span> button without selecting any option;
                                    </li>
                                    <li>When a candidate click on a particular question, it takes some time for the question to appear. The time lost is not deducted from the total time allotted for the test;</li>
                                </ul>
                                <div class="declaration-txt">
                                    <input type="checkbox" />
                                    <label>
                                        &nbsp; Declaration : I have read and understood all the above instructions. I agree that I have not brought with me any prohibited item like mobile phone etc. to the examination hall. I agree that in
                                        case of non-compliance of the instructions, I will be disqualified from taking the examination.
                                    </label>
                                </div>
                                <div class="ready-to-begin">
                                    <button class="ready-btn" role="button">I am ready to begin</button>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </body>
    <script src="js/jquery-3.2.1.min.js"></script>
    <script src="js/bootstrap.min.js"></script>
    <script src="javascript/login.js"></script>
</html>
